From: ROCKNIX/DUCKTALE
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: restore fatal L2-entry timeout on suspend (7.0 behavior)

7.1 made PCIe L2-entry timeout non-fatal (warn + proceed to power-off)
vs 7.0 (err + return). On the Odin 3 the WLAN endpoint intermittently
misses the 10ms L2 ack at system suspend; 7.1 then tears the controller
down in an inconsistent L2 state and a USB-C VBUS event during that sleep
hangs the NoC via the half-collapsed PCIe controller -> hard wedge. 7.0
(identical fw/DT) never wedges. Restore the 7.0 fatal-on-timeout path.

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -1256,13 +1256,9 @@
 				PCIE_PME_TO_L2_TIMEOUT_US/10,
 				PCIE_PME_TO_L2_TIMEOUT_US, false, pci);
 	if (ret) {
-		/*
-		 * Failure is non-fatal since spec r7.0, sec 5.3.3.2.1,
-		 * recommends proceeding with L2/L3 sequence even if one or more
-		 * devices do not respond with PME_TO_Ack after 10ms timeout.
-		 */
-		dev_warn(pci->dev, "Timeout waiting for L2 entry! LTSSM: 0x%x\n", val);
-		ret = 0;
+		/* Only log message when LTSSM isn't in DETECT or POLL */
+		dev_err(pci->dev, "Timeout waiting for L2 entry! LTSSM: 0x%x\n", val);
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	/*
